{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1051106-victorian-changeling-campaign-set-in-hong-kong-1860","id":1051106,"title":"\"Victorian\" Changeling campaign set in Hong Kong 1860","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-18T12:40:21-08:00","id":1051106,"title":"\"Victorian\" Changeling campaign set in Hong Kong 1860","content":"So, I'm in the process of reading the Victorian Lost from 2012 and I've decided to do a mid-19th-century Changeling 1e game, EXCEPT instead of the cliche London, I'm setting it in British Colonial Hong Kong. There will be other supernaturals used in the game: mages, vampires, werewolves, promethians... but the focus is mainly changeling.<br /> <br /> Any recommendations you guys might make for running such a game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T01:17:52-08:00","id":1055129,"title":"","content":"Really? No one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T02:27:08-08:00","id":1055143,"title":"","content":"I know nothing of the setting or what you are hoping to do with your story. I would imagine that that's the same reason nobody else has responded previously. Try asking something more specific about it, and see if that drives some discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T18:17:36-07:00","id":1064105,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a wonderful idea, Hong Kong has always been an enigmatic place and a Changeling story based around it would be very interesting. I'd suggest you do research on Colonial Hong Kong and get an idea of what life was like back then use historical figures to create archetypes for your NPCs and local legends or stories to get an idea for plotlines. I might be interested in trying this out if you get it off the ground though I can be a bit unreliable when playing online at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2015-inspectorjavert","name":"inspectorjavert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T01:11:16-07:00","id":1067443,"title":"","content":"What role will the recently ended Opium Wars play in your chronicle? What view did the Changeling Courts hold on the conflict and what role, if any, did they play?<br /> \u200bMore importantly, how did the Keepers play it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:00:36-07:00","id":1067624,"title":"","content":"I absolutely adore Victorian Hong Kong as a setting and wish you the best with it. If you want some inspiration, I think the first episode of the second season of Ripper Street revolves around a corrupt police inspector out of HK and those he's hurt that hunted him back to London.<br /> <br /> In my headcanon, modern HK has the Directional Courts in a cold war with the Seasonals that the British back then; if you go back a century, that conflict is likely still hot, with Lost gang wars in the streets and on the sea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 03-24-2017, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T18:26:13-07:00","id":1067878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1051106-victorian-changeling-campaign-set-in-hong-kong-1860?p=1067443#post1067443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What role will the recently ended Opium Wars play in your chronicle? What view did the Changeling Courts hold on the conflict and what role, if any, did they play?<br /> \u200bMore importantly, how did the Keepers play it?</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I've always thought should be explored is if changelings were using goblin fruit to make drugs or augment other drugs. Maybe someone is making a new opium using goblin fruit and the courts don't like it since it might attract the Keepers. Or maybe the seasonal courts are selling and the directional don't want them to we could have Opium Wars II: Attack of the Changelings!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2015-inspectorjavert","name":"inspectorjavert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T17:06:09-07:00","id":1068123,"title":"","content":"I don't know why I can never get this forum to send me notifications, just logged in for something else and was pleasantly surprised to see activity in this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1051106-victorian-changeling-campaign-set-in-hong-kong-1860?p=1067443#post1067443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What role will the recently ended Opium Wars play in your chronicle? What view did the Changeling Courts hold on the conflict and what role, if any, did they play?<br /> \u200bMore importantly, how did the Keepers play it?</div> </div> </div> </div> The recently ended opium wars plays a huge role. You have a third of the population addicted to opium, including the changeling population, resulting in more changelings falling to clarity 0. The seasonal courts came with the British colonists and they are in conflict with the directional courts.<br /> I don't know yet how the Keepers play it. Suggestions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1051106-victorian-changeling-campaign-set-in-hong-kong-1860?p=1067624#post1067624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely adore Victorian Hong Kong as a setting and wish you the best with it. If you want some inspiration, I think the first episode of the second season of Ripper Street revolves around a corrupt police inspector out of HK and those he's hurt that hunted him back to London.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll check that out/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my headcanon, modern HK has the Directional Courts in a cold war with the Seasonals that the British back then; if you go back a century, that conflict is likely still hot, with Lost gang wars in the streets and on the sea. </div> </div> </div> A similar direction as to what I'm aiming for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inspectorjavert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1051106-victorian-changeling-campaign-set-in-hong-kong-1860?p=1067878#post1067878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've always thought should be explored is if changelings were using goblin fruit to make drugs or augment other drugs. Maybe someone is making a new opium using goblin fruit and the courts don't like it since it might attract the Keepers. Or maybe the seasonal courts are selling and the directional don't want them to we could have Opium Wars II: Attack of the Changelings!</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T17:51:35-07:00","id":1248581,"title":"","content":"Does your local library system have anything on Chinese Fairy Tales? Anything you find will be as new to your players as it is to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T08:34:32-07:00","id":1249147,"title":"","content":"I might suggest looking into the hurt locker psychic vampires for their ability to &quot;drink&quot; the breath of people. I've heard that is reflected in eastern mythology. 1e vampire had a type of vampire that functioned different. <br /> <br /> Otherwise? Pretty much open a history book is the best advise I can give. Twist events to have supernatural causes. Reinterpret key historical figuess. Look into eastern mythology that lines up close with western fey mythology for inspieation on the fey and the hedge. Explore if players are local or foreign and the issues related to that from language, culture or perspections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}